  "question": {
    "text": "A very long solenoid is made out of a wire with <math><mi>n</mi></math> turns per unit length. The radius of the cylinder is <math><mi>a</mi></math> and is negligible compared to its length <math><mi>l</mi></math>. The interior of the cylinder is filled with materials such that the linear magnetic permeability varies with the distance <math><mi>r</mi></math> from axis according to<br />\r<math><mi>μ</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced></math><br />\rThe self-inductance of the solenoid is",
